  {
   "id": "BeEiV7Q1aJkJ",
   "from": "Joon Lim",
   "author": "3dc89d3147ac0901",
   "date": "2014-06-12T01:12:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: Directly access to a tab",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, it works! Thank you so much Joe.<div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Anyone, who wants to try Joe&#39;s code, can just run the code below..</div><div>--- </div><div><div>runApp(list( ui = fluidPage(</div>\r\n<div>  tabsetPanel(id = &quot;tabset&quot;,</div><div>              tabPanel(value = &quot;tab1&quot;, &quot;One&quot;),</div><div>              tabPanel(value = &quot;tab2&quot;, &quot;Two&quot;),</div><div>              tabPanel(value = &quot;insight&quot;, &quot;Three&quot;)</div>\r\n<div>  )</div><div>), server = function(input, output, session) {</div><div>  # On startup, read the URL parameter</div><div>  queryParams &lt;- parseQueryString(isolate(session$clientData$url_search))</div><div>  if (&#39;tab&#39; %in% names(queryParams))</div>\r\n<div>    updateTabsetPanel(session, &#39;tabset&#39;, selected = paste0(&#39;tab&#39;, queryParams[[&#39;tab&#39;]]))</div><div>}))</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 11, 2014 at 6:52 PM, Joe Cheng <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">j...@rstudio.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Try doing something like this:<div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/5427d6f264408abf3049\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/5427d6f264408abf3049&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792403474770000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1NjRGGjKzo6psbxosNqBX6\">https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/5427d6f264408abf3049</a><br>\r\n</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">\r\n\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 11, 2014 at 12:03 PM, Joon Lim <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jl...@motorola.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Shiny team,<div><br></div><div>How are you? I am using the fluidPage and absolutePanel for my dashboard and also gave id to tabsetPanel and name to each tabPanel. I am trying to find a way to access to <span style=\"line-height:17px\">one of my tabPanels directly from http link? Anyone knows how I can do this?</span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"line-height:17px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Thanks,</span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Joon</span></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus